' H(CH2)    LEIP LAB   EVAL-JAN23 N.C. Fleming, A.I. Hawari        '/
'                      DIST-                                       '/
'----ENDF/B-VIII       MATERIAL  37                                '/
'-----THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                              '/
'------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                               '/
'                                                                  '/
' Temperatures = 15 20 25 50 77 196 233 293.6 300 303 313 323      '/
' 333 343 350 K                                                    '/
'                                                                  '/
' HISTORY                                                          '/
' -------                                                          '/
' This library was produced by the Low Energy Interactions         '/
' Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University (USA)    '/
' using the same model as ENDF/B-VIII.0. Fifteen temperatures are  '/
' available in this library. The inelastic scattering cross        '/
' section libraries for H in CH2 (Polyethylene) were developed     '/
' using molecular dynamics methods [1,2]. This material is a       '/
' polymer.  The incoherent elastic cross section is significant,   '/
' so the MT = 2 section for elastic scattering is present. The     '/
' Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to     '/
' produce MT = 2 and MT = 4 data [3].  By convention, MAT=37 and   '/
' ZA=137 are used for H in Polyethylene.                           '/
'                                                                  '/
' |-----------------------------------------------------|          '/
' | ISOTOPE |   MASS [4]   | FREE ATOM [4] |  ABUNDANCE |          '/
' |         | (neut. wt.)  |       (b)     |     (%)    |          '/
' |-----------------------------------------------------|          '/
' |   H-1   | 9.991673E-01 |  2.043608E+01 | 99.9885 [5]|          '/
' |   H-2   | 1.996800E+00 |  3.395000E+00 |  0.0115 [5]|          '/
' |-----------------------------------------------------|          '/
' |  H-nat  | 9.992820E-01 |  2.043412E+01              |          '/
' |-----------------------------------------------------|          '/
'                                                                  '/
' REFERENCES                                                       '/
' ----------                                                       '/
' 1. A.I. Hawari, "Modern Techniques in Inelastic Thermal Neutron  '/
'    Scattering Analysis," Nuclear Data Sheets 118, 172 (2014).    '/
'                                                                  '/
' 2. A.I. Hawari, A. Petersen, Y. Zhu, et al., "Development of a   '/
'    Thermal Neutron Scattering Law for Polyethylene Using         '/
'    Molecular Dynamics Simulations." Transactions of the American '/
'    Nuclear Society, v. 115, Nov 6-10, 2016.                      '/
'                                                                  '/
' 3. N.C. Fleming, et al., "FLASSH 1.0: Thermal Scattering Law     '/
'    Evaluation and Cross Section Generation for Reactor Physics   '/
'    Applications," Nucl. Sci. and Eng. (2023).                    '/
'                                                                  '/
' 4. D.A. Brown, et al., "ENDF/B-VIII.0: The 8th Major Release of  '/
